Hello folks.  When using a 'besag' model in INLA, the ID column in summary.random goes from 0 to N-1, whereas the ID column for an iid random effect go from 1 to N, as in the example below.

When specifying linear combinations, am I correct in thinking I should use indexes 1 to N for the besag part? If I want to add the independent and structured effect for region 1 I should do

mylincomb$region.struct$idx=1
mylincomb$region$idx=1

rather than

mylincomb$region.struct$idx=0
mylincomb$region$idx=1

?

'day

p
data(Germany)
g = system.file("demodata/germany.graph", package="INLA")
source(system.file("demodata/Bym-map.R", package="INLA"))
summary(Germany)

## just make a duplicated column
Germany = cbind(Germany,region.struct=Germany$region)

# standard BYM model (without covariates)
formula1 = Y ~ f(region.struct,model="besag",graph.file=g) +
               f(region,model="iid")

result1  =  inla(formula1,family="poisson",data=Germany,E=E)

result1$summary.random$region.struct[1:4,1:4]

result1$summary.random$region[1:4,1:4]

